  "live_records": {
    "q-50897": {
      "dom_id": "step-q50897",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $-2+\\frac{8}{3!}-\\frac{32}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-2$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2) & =(-2)-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(-2)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡2 & =-2+\\frac{8}{3!}-\\frac{32}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
