    "q-103098": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103098",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}) & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}-\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(5\\pi /6)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(5\\pi /6)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-103098-a",
