    "q-83287": {
      "dom_id": "step-q83287",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $-3+\\frac{27}{3!}-\\frac{243}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-3$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3) & =(-3)-\\frac{(-3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(-3)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3 & =-3+\\frac{27}{3!}-\\frac{243}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-83287-a",
