    "q-50922": {
      "dom_id": "step-q50922",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\pi $ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =\\pi -\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{\\pi }^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{\\pi }^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
