    "q-350677": {
      "dom_id": "step-q350677",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,?$\n\nThe sum of the series is\n{{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) & =1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ 0 & =1-\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{(3\\pi /2)}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,(3\\pi /2)^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $0.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
