    "q-103114": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103114",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$1-\\frac{25}{2!}+\\frac{625}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯=$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{x}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=5$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5 & =1-\\frac{{5}^{2}}{2!}+\\frac{{5}^{4}}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡5 & =1-\\frac{25}{2!}+\\frac{625}{4!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}\\,{5}^{2n}}{(2n)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\operatorname{cos}⁡5.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
